  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 31 to 32; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  max-version 32 is below the oldest maintained major (33, the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), so the release covers only servers that no longer receive fixes.",
        "  min-version 31 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is weekplanner, the checkout directory is weekplanner-nextcloud.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: composer.json requires php ^8.1; appinfo/info.xml declares no php dependency.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.cjs, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.cjs: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "script-without-workflow",
      "lines": [
        "package.json declares the script test, which no installed workflow runs.",
        "  The template node-test of nextcloud/.github runs test: make workflows-install W=node-test",
        "  A check that no workflow runs on a pull request catches only what the contributor who remembers to run it catches."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "2 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/stylelint-config, @vue/test-utils.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 79 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL-3.0-or-later (appinfo/info.xml, package.json, composer.json).",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "versions-agree",
      "lines": [
        "Version 1.6.5 in appinfo/info.xml and package.json."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "The 4 links of appinfo/info.xml answer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 20 stated in .nvmrc, within package.json engines.node >=20.0.0.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "pnpm-lock.yaml in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
